course: dictionary
lesson: 3661
title: Same word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a place, and also the work that happens there. A fishery is a place where fish are caught or bred, like a part of the sea or a fish farm. It can also mean the business or industry of catching fish.
explain: Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits. «A blue fish label on packets shows fish from a fishery checked as well managed.» Here the fishery is the place the fish came from, and the label tells you it was well run.
explain: Ask yourself: is the sentence talking about a place or about a job? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A fishery is a place where fish are caught or bred.
fact: A fishery can also be the business or industry of catching fish.
fact: A «sustainable» fishery catches fish carefully, so there are still fish in the future.
fact: Coastal towns in Canada, Ireland, Iceland and New Zealand often depend on their fisheries.
fact: The plural of fishery is fisheries.
exercise: «A blue fish label on packets shows fish from a fishery checked as well managed.» What is a fishery in this sentence? | *A place where fish are caught or bred | A label printed on packets | A boat that sails far out to sea | A kind of fish sold in shops
exercise: Which phrase describes a fishery that is well managed so the fish will last for the future? | Village shop | Fishing hat | *Sustainable fishery | Ocean storm
exercise: What is the plural of fishery? | *Fisheries | Fishes | Fisherys | Fisheries' fish
test: «The fishery off the coast of Iceland closed for the winter.» What does fishery mean here? | *A place or business where fish are caught | A shop that sells fish and chips | A storm at sea | A museum about fish
test: Why would a shop show a label saying its fish came from a well-managed fishery? | So the fish stay frozen for longer | So the packets are heavier | So the fish can talk to the shoppers | *So shoppers know the fish were caught carefully
exam: Which sentence uses fishery to mean the business of catching fish? | We walked along the fishery and saw the waves | *The fishery employs three hundred people in the village | The fishery was painted bright blue last summer | Mum dropped the fishery into the sink
